#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:5 db4041230c894ed79cb0896f49ddb94a
msgid "Indoor Flying Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:7 240ea9af706f4c7f8672790f1e581a20
msgid ""
"This article provides guidelines for flying your multicopter inside "
"without any position or velocity source (e.g. no GPS, no optical flow). "
"For indoor flight using a non-GPS position or velocity source please "
"refer to the :ref:`Non-GPS Navigation <common-non-gps-navigation-landing-"
"page>` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:12 5fbd4d9689d54617ae378acb7233bb8a
msgid ""
"When flying indoors make sure you have plenty of space and follow safety "
"procedures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:14 398fb8cc4ae7476e864097302eeacbfa
msgid "GPS does not work indoors and needs to be disabled (no exceptions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:17 856bfb826e76404493d81ccf4dc4b63e
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:19 ef30548a0a15428f8d1d7a7eb97d48b4
msgid ""
"The main point note when flying indoors is that Global Positioning "
"Systems will not work. Even if you see that you have the correct number "
"of satellites and a low HDOP, this is due to multipathing of the signals "
"from the satellites. This means the single is being reflected to the "
"antenna via walls, windows and other surfaces from outside. If you look "
"at the position on a map you will see that the location will not match "
"your current location, or will be drifting, at time many meters or even "
"1000s of metres from your location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:29 03e65adc7d1840fcb6d015655680bf66
msgid "Stabilize"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:31 719807734bd443a6a157e4a94066b40a
msgid ""
":ref:`Stabilize <stabilize-mode>` mode does not use GPS, and has the "
"least problems, but the pilot will need good control of the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:35 c89185f39b784dec8e5ac638cf35eab4
msgid "Altitude Hold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:37 db4fc7b41b0541459cd7a1a8ff1524ac
msgid ""
":ref:`Altitude Hold <altholdmode>` mode use the barometer to hold a "
"specific altitude. The barometer relies on a constant air pressure. Air-"
"pressure in a room can change due to doors opening or closing. Also "
"climate control devices like fans and air-conditioning will also cause "
"pressure changes. The likely outcome is a sudden crash in the floor or "
"ceiling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:45 671b83d0e68b4b26ba2a0cc8abda4eea
msgid "Sonar or Lidar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:47 3d2c0e1eea5e446aa18e87d5f2a66cbb
msgid ""
"Using a downward facing :ref:`sonar or lidar <common-rangefinder-"
"landingpage>` when flying in :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` can help avoid "
"sudden changes in altitude causing crashes into the floor or ceiling.  "
"See :ref:`Surface Tracking <terrain-following-manual-modes>` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:50 e4cde8a5fce94fb98a2f854629cb1607
msgid "Safe Indoor Flying Dos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:52 4a56a63895c745a69e325d68164623c1
msgid "Disable the GPS by setting :ref:`GPS1_TYPE<GPS1_TYPE>` to 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:53 45aec2065ea04c0e898f5d65125015e0
msgid ""
"Configure the :ref:`battery failsafe <failsafe-battery>` to \"Land\" by "
"setting :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT <BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:54 dabc23392c404f4db21d0a422548172e
msgid ""
"Configure the :ref:`radio failsafe <radio-failsafe>` to \"Enabled always "
"Land\" by setting :ref:`FS_THR_ENABLE <FS_THR_ENABLE>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:55 dbe24f90f01f40d2af90225f2fd2176e
msgid ""
"Disable the :ref:`fence <common-geofencing-landing-page>` by setting "
":ref:`FENCE_ENABLE <FENCE_ENABLE>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:56 726175733cf448adadeb6704722deac4
msgid "Use a downward facing sonar or lidar (if available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:59 e28fa383a9b946d68d7d82b5791a7f10
msgid "Safe Indoor Flying Don'ts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:61 1ed2b54678354e1dafffa49d08d9d005
msgid ""
"Don't fly in small confined spaces. Use common sense, flying inside a "
"warehouse with a high roof = OK, bedroom = not OK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:63 8e027d79dd9247fbb245c5e62d2383ca
msgid "Don't use Auto\\* modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:65 ae8775088a1d4913ba042e83bc3b7924
msgid ""
"\\* Autonomous and semi-autonomous modes requires GPS (e.g. :ref:`Loiter "
"<loiter-mode>`, :ref:`Guided <ac2_guidedmode>`, :ref:`Auto <auto-mode>`, "
":ref:`RTL <rtl-mode>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/indoor-flying.rst:67 4983b8477efd4c15b8cc3a382354a497
msgid ""
"\\*\\* Non-autonomous modes include :ref:`Stabilize <stabilize-mode>` and"
" :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>`"
msgstr ""

